### Corrective Control

A corrective control was tested by validating Windows' response to an application failure and by creating a simple PowerShell-based file integrity verification process.

- Triggered a controlled system crash using Sysinternals NotMyFault to observe Windows' built-in recovery mechanism.
- Generated a SHA-256 hash for a monitored text file.
- Modified the file to simulate unauthorized changes.
- Compared the current file hash against the known-good hash.
- Restored the original file contents after detecting the integrity change.
- Automated the verification process using PowerShell scripts.

> **Note:** No screenshots were captured for the corrective control portion of the lab.

